---
/**
 * Notes for hosts that use a package already in the picker.
 * The visible panel follows the same chartkit.framework / ck-fw chip as the install sample.
 */
---

<div class="host-notes">
  <div data-stack-panel="react">
    <h2>Same package</h2>
    <p>
      Preact uses <code>@chartkitdev/react</code>. Alias <code>react</code> and <code>react-dom</code> to <code>preact/compat</code>, then render <code>Chart</code> as in React.
    </p>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>vite</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`resolve: {
  alias: {
    react: "preact/compat",
    "react-dom": "preact/compat",
  },
}`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
    <p>Next.js App Router and Remix or React Router use that same component. App Router can print the SVG on the server.</p>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>tsx</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`import { renderToString } from "react-dom/server";
import { Chart } from "@chartkitdev/react";

const html = renderToString(<Chart spec={spec} />);`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>tsx</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`import { Chart } from "@chartkitdev/react";

export default function Panel() {
  return <Chart spec={spec} />;
}`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div data-stack-panel="vue">
    <h2>Nuxt</h2>
    <p>
      Nuxt is Vue. <code>@chartkitdev/vue</code> includes the SVG during SSR. <code>renderToString</code> from <code>@chartkitdev/vue/ssr</code> is the HTML string.
    </p>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>vue</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`<script setup>
import { Chart } from "@chartkitdev/vue";
</script>

<template>
  <Chart :spec="spec" />
</template>`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div data-stack-panel="svelte">
    <h2>SvelteKit</h2>
    <p>SvelteKit SSR includes the SVG. There is no second package.</p>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>svelte</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`<script>
  import { Chart } from "@chartkitdev/svelte";
</script>

<Chart {spec} />`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div data-stack-panel="vanilla">
    <h2>Server HTML</h2>
    <p>
      htmx and Eleventy have no component compiler. <code>renderToString</code> from <code>@chartkitdev/vanilla</code> is the SVG. Drop it in the response. When an htmx swap should take pointers, use <code>&lt;chart-kit&gt;</code> from <code>@chartkitdev/element</code>, or call <code>mount()</code>.
    </p>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>js</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`import { renderToString } from "@chartkitdev/vanilla";

const svg = renderToString(spec);`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption>js</figcaption>
      <pre><code>{`import { renderToString } from "@chartkitdev/vanilla";

eleventyConfig.addShortcode("chart", (spec) => renderToString(spec));`}</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>
